  "notes": [
    "Complete list: 17 actions (src/actions/actions.ts set-param, src/actions/cursor.ts 10 actions, src/actions/clip.ts 6 actions) and 2 advanced feedbacks (src/feedbacks.ts). Definitions are rebuilt on every composition update (src/index.ts updateInstance), but their options do not depend on the composition.",
    "Third-party repository (chabad360); the manifest repository field names bitfocus/companion-module-resolume-ws. Not verified whether the module is listed in the Companion module store. The last commit is from 2024-06-03.",
    "Protocol: Resolume Arena WebSocket API through the \"resolume\" npm package (src/resolume.ts); config fields host (default 127.0.0.1) and httpPort (number 1-65535, step 1, default 7003) (src/config.ts). Variables (src/variables.ts) are not catalogued.",
    "Layer, column and clip positions are text inputs with the regex NumberOrVariable = /^(\\d+|\\$\\(.+\\))/ (src/actions/actions.ts:11; not anchored at the end, so \"1abc\" also matches) and useVariables. Values are 1-based; most actions subtract 1 internally and send +1 again, while select-layer and select-clip send the entered number unchanged.",
    "All \"Selected ...\" checkboxes default to false; the position fields have isVisible (options) => !options.selected (recorded in visibleWhen) except in select-layer, select-clip and connect-column, which have no such checkbox. When ticked, the module uses the clip or layer last selected in Resolume (instance.selectedClipLayer/selectedClipColumn/selectedLayer).",
    "Dropdown ids are numbers (0, 1, 2, ...) as in the source; the callbacks check typeof === \"number\". toggle-playdirection and toggle-clip-resize step the current index +1 and wrap to From when it passes To.",
    "Source quirk: clear-layer with \"Selected Layer\" ticked and no layer selected (selectedLayer -1) sends a trigger for layer 0; most other actions return silently when the clip does not exist in the received composition.",
    "Built on @companion-module/base ~1.8.0: option values cannot be expressions."
  ]
}
